WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.020
Going to the market can be
hell for Nigerian women

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:12.099
They are often touched,
groped and insulted by men

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:14.790
One woman
has launched #MarketMarch

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.349
a protest movement that
wants to stop the harassment

00:00:18.349 --> 00:00:26.050
"So many Nigerian feminists unite over their
experience at the market, passing through

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:31.749
most of the major markets in cities in Nigeria
is a traumatizing and terrifying experience.

00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:36.030
From when they were children, young girls
and even as adult women.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.900
It's something I expect when I'm going to
the market.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.260
And I decided something needed to be done
about it.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.670
Every citizen has a right to protest."

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.730
At the first protest
some men were aggressive

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:53.020
They insulted the women and
threw stones at them

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:58.130
"We must touch,
we must touch!"

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:04.970
"They really do not believe that we should
resist them touching us.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.200
There is a very strong sense of entitlement.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.060
In any possible way you can think of, they
will express it.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.060
Whether they're pulling...

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:18.619
I heard stories where they slapped people
who resisted, where they slapped women who

00:01:18.619 --> 00:01:19.619
resisted.

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:25.930
So the problem is entitlement and expressing
that entitlement, depending on the market

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:31.420
man you encounter and how engrained it is
in him."

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.859
Damilola says the march
was a success

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:41.000
"So many women are tired, they're frustrated
with their position in society.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.549
And they want better.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:46.439
They are taking matters into their own hands.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.539
And it's only going to get better from there.

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:50.719
It has started.

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:55.829
The momentum has begun and there is no going
back."

